# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: the entropy PD fills both seed
# rings; seed_flood, taking seeds as fast as it can for 2 s, is held to its
# rate (its count, the line before, is not checked: it differs every run),
# while polite_consumer gets every seed it asks for within its own.
NOWAYOS: entropy: starting
NOWAYOS: entropy: virtio-rng on transport 8, claimed to give 8 bits a byte
NOWAYOS: entropy: start-up tests passed over the first 1024 bytes, which were discarded
NOWAYOS: entropy: seed ring 0 full: 4 seeds
NOWAYOS: entropy: seed ring 1 full: 4 seeds
NOWAYOS: polite-consumer: starting
NOWAYOS: seed-flood: starting
NOWAYOS: polite-consumer: got every seed it asked for: 5, one each 200 ms
NOWAYOS: seed-flood: held to its rate: a ring's worth, then 10 seeds a second

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: a fault, a panic, a PD
# giving up, a failed health test or a refused seed.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!health test failed
!a seed refused
!too few bytes
